Hey, I was on a vacation, so I was away. Your changes are fine. I know I'm dragging it a little but just only one concern is left.  Huge negative values overflows, and  aren't caught.

```
127.0.0.1:6379> GET foo
"a"
127.0.0.1:6379> EXPIRE foo -9999999999999999
(integer) 1
127.0.0.1:6379> GET foo
"a"
127.0.0.1:6379> TTL foo
(integer) 8446744073709543
```

The only way I could think to fix this is doing double-checking the time in the expire function. We had discussed double-checking (earlier)[https://github.com/redis/redis/pull/8287#pullrequestreview-564301416], but still shedding the light.

```c
void expireGenericCommand(client *c, long long basetime, int unit) {
...
    if (checkAlreadyExpired(when)) {
